    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `clean_orders` in `app/clean.py`, and all 5 tests pass (`pytest -q`).\n\nWhat it does:\n- **Copies first:** it works on `df.copy()`, so the input frame isn't changed.\n- **Text columns:** it treats both `object` and string-dtype columns as text. The project pins pandas 3.0.6, where text read from CSV gets the new `str` dtype instead of `object`, so checking only for `object` would miss every column. It strips leading and trailing whitespace, then turns empty strings (including ones that were only whitespace) into missing values.\n- **Mixed `object` columns:** only actual strings are stripped. Numbers and other non-string values stay as they are, and the column keeps its dtype. A plain `.str.strip()` would have turned those values into NaN.\n- **`qty`:** missing values are filled with 0. Other numeric columns, like `price`, keep their missing values.\n\nI also added `tests/test_clean_orders.py`. It covers stripping and blank-to-missing, the `qty` fill with `price` left alone, the input staying unchanged with dtypes kept, and an `object` column with mixed values. No dependencies were added."
  },
